{%- comment -%} ===================== PS5 (journey 4) ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-platforms-ps5" data-group="Connect" data-title="Playing on PS5" data-time="6 min" data-journey="4"
  data-keywords="ps5 playstation 5 setup connect wire auth dongle console">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Connect</p>
    <h1>Playing on PS5</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Wire up your EXO, choose PS5 in the app and check it works.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">PS5</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">6 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The PS5 auth dongle (in the PS5 version box).</li>
      <li>The cables from the box, plus a second HDMI cable if you want the HDMI loop (you can reuse your PS5's own).</li>
      <li>The <a href="#p-start-install-the-app">ZeroStick app installed</a> on your phone.</li>
      <li>Your mouse, keyboard or controller, with its USB cable or wireless dongle.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--1-plug-in-your-controls">
    <h2>1. Plug in your controls</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Plug your mouse (or its wireless dongle) into a front port.</li>
      <li>Plug your keyboard into another front port.</li>
      <li>Plug in a controller with a USB cable, if you use one.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-front.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="265" loading="lazy"
        alt="The front of the EXO. One USB-C port on the left and three USB-A ports, for controllers, a mouse and a keyboard.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.1 — The front of the EXO: one USB-C port and three USB-A ports</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>Any front port works for any device: 1 USB-C and 3 USB-A. Need more ports? A USB hub works.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Bluetooth controllers aren't supported at launch. Connect your controller with a USB cable.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--2-connect-authentication">
    <h2>2. Connect authentication</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Plug the included PS5 auth dongle into <b>AUTH</b> on the back.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-auth.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the AUTH USB-A port marked.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.2 — AUTH: the included PS5 auth dongle goes here</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>The PS5 checks that a controller is genuine. The dongle answers that check. Leave it plugged in whenever you play on PS5.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--3-connect-to-the-console">
    <h2>3. Connect to the console</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Turn on your PS5.</li>
      <li>Plug a USB-C to USB-A cable into <b>CONSOLE</b> on the EXO.</li>
      <li>Plug the other end into a USB port on your PS5.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-console.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the CONSOLE USB-C port marked. It goes to your console or PC.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.3 — CONSOLE: the cable to your PS5</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>The EXO turns on by itself and the logo lights up. It gets its power from this cable.</p>
    <figure class="m2-media">{% render 'zs-exo2-visual', view: 'ports-back' %}<figcaption>Figure PS5.4 — Back of the EXO: AUTH takes the dongle, CONSOLE goes to the PS5.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--4-connect-hdmi">
    <h2>4. Connect HDMI (optional)</h2>
    <p>Skip this step if you don't need automatic gun detection yet.</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Unplug the HDMI cable from your TV and plug it into <b>HDMI IN</b> on the EXO.</li>
      <li>Plug a second HDMI cable into <b>HDMI OUT</b>.</li>
      <li>Plug the other end into your TV or monitor.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-hdmi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="599" loading="lazy"
        alt="The two HDMI ports on the back of the EXO. HDMI IN takes the cable from your console. HDMI OUT goes to your TV.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.5 — HDMI IN from the console, HDMI OUT to the TV</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>More detail: <a href="#p-platforms-hdmi">Connect HDMI</a>.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>First time setting up? Wiring is done. Now <a href="#p-start-pair-your-phone">pair your phone</a> (step 5 of 12), then come back for step 5 below.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--5-choose-the-platform">
    <h2>5. Choose the platform in the app</h2>
    <p>New configs ask where they play. If you picked <b>PlayStation 5</b> there, just check it here.</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b> under the game picture.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Device</b>.</li>
      <li>Scroll to <b>Connection Method</b> and tap the console row (B).</li>
      <li>In <b>Console Connection</b>, tap the arrows until it shows <b>PlayStation 5</b>. It saves at once.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-platform-3-m2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="935" loading="lazy"
        alt="Device page. A: Connection Method. B: the console row reading PlayStation 5, Joystick plus Mouse. C: What you play with: Auto, Mouse plus Keyboard, Controller, Joystick plus Mouse.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.6 — Settings › Device › Connection Method</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Connection Method</b></td><td>The console this config plays on.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>PlayStation 5</b></td><td>Tap to change the console.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>What you play with</b></td><td>Leave it on <b>Auto</b> unless you have a reason.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>It saves the moment you tap it. If this is the config that's playing, the console connection restarts in about a second. The PS5 sees the controller unplug and plug back in. The EXO itself doesn't restart.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cc-pick-ps5.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="433" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Console and Network Connection panel. Console Connection shows PlayStation 5, with arrows either side to change it.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.7 — Console Connection panel on PlayStation 5</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cc-ps5-chosen.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="356" loading="lazy"
        alt="Back on the Device page, the Connection Method card now reads PlayStation 5, Joystick plus Mouse. 1: the console row.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.8 — Connection Method after you pick PlayStation 5</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>PlayStation 5</b></td><td>Your console. Tap again to change it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--6-set-your-in-game-settings">
    <h2>6. Set your in-game settings</h2>
    <p>Your aim feels right only when your game's own settings match what the EXO expects. The app lists them for each game.</p>
    <p>On HOME, tap <b>Set your in-game settings for proper aim</b> to open the list.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-sheet.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Your game settings sheet, marked REQUIRED, with the rows to set in the game. 1: your stick sensitivity boxes. 2: Your in-game FOV. 3: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.9 — Your game settings sheet, a mouse config (MW4)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Your stick sensitivity</b></td><td>Type the sensitivity you set in the game (4.00 recommended).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Your in-game FOV</b></td><td>Type the field of view you play at.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>Why these must match the game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Follow <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--7-check-it-worked">
    <h2>7. Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>EXO:</b> the logo is lit in your config's colour.</li>
        <li><b>App:</b> the EXO card on HOME shows <b>Connected</b> and <b>PS5 Mode</b>.</li>
        <li><b>PS5:</b> your mouse, keyboard or controller moves around the PS5 menus.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-ps5--controller-not-working">PS5 problems</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--8-use-menus-with-pass-through">
    <h2>8. Use menus with Pass-through</h2>
    <p>Press <span class="m2-key">1</span> + <span class="m2-key">5</span> on your keyboard to pause your config for menus, chat and typing. Press it again, or tap <b>Turn off Passthrough</b> on HOME, to come back.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-pt-home.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1407" loading="lazy"
        alt="HOME while Pass-through is on: Passthrough mode active, to the PS5, your config is paused. 1: the Turn off Passthrough button, with or press 1 plus 5 under it.">
      <figcaption>Figure PS5.10 — HOME while Pass-through is on</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Turn off Passthrough</b></td><td>Back to your config. Pressing 1 + 5 again does the same.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>More: <a href="#p-app-passthrough">Pass-through</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-platforms-ps5--9-if-it-didnt-work">
    <h2>9. If it didn't work</h2>
    <ul class="m2-cards">
      <li><a class="m2-card" href="#p-help-ps5--controller-not-working"><b>Nothing happens on the PS5</b><span>The PS5 doesn't respond to your controls.</span></a></li>
      <li><a class="m2-card" href="#p-help-ps5--wrong-mode"><b>HOME shows the wrong mode</b><span>It says Xbox Mode or PC Mode.</span></a></li>
      <li><a class="m2-card" href="#p-help-app-connection--cant-find-exo"><b>The app can't find the EXO</b><span>Pairing or Bluetooth trouble.</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>

